Implement unified NF_LEDGER schema per NF_LEDGER_SCHEMA_v1.md (Phase 1, Q-NF-SCHEMA-01):

1. Enhance molt_cycle.py with NF_LEDGER reading capability:
   - read_nf_ledger(): Load and parse ledger, index PIN/RESOLVE by target
   - join_pin_resolve_pairs(): Match PIN (prediction) with RESOLVE (outcome)
   - calculate_brier_scores(): Compute Brier score per predictor and overall
   - count_resolved(): Report how many predictions have been resolved
   - CLI: --read-only --nf <path> for integration testing

2. Add comprehensive integration tests (test_nf_schema_integration.py):
   - test_read_nf_ledger_mesh_pins(): Verify mesh pins ledger loading (165 entries, 75 PIN targets)
   - test_join_pin_resolve_pairs_with_synthetic_data(): PIN/RESOLVE joining logic
   - test_brier_calculation(): Brier score math (perfect/bad/uncertain predictions)
   - test_count_resolved(): Resolved prediction counting
   - test_falsifier_q_nf_schema_01(): Falsifier compliance (nf_resolved > 0 with RESOLVE entries)

3. Create genesis record (M-20260910-GENESIS) for molt tracking:
   - Appends TIER0 molt entry to NF_LEDGER.jsonl
   - Marks NF_LEDGER v1.0 initialization
   - Properly hash-chained from last mesh pin entry
   - Foundation for forward molt ledger entries

Schema resolution (4 incompatibilities per spec):
  · nf_ledger_v0_1 → v1.0: Extend with prediction/outcome/window/ratification
  · molt_cycle events → v1.0: Molt entries ARE NF_LEDGER entries (no separate file)
  · specimen_intake → v1.0: Specimen outcomes feed as Brier input
  · breadcrumbs → v1.0: Trace/audit embedded in NF_LEDGER records

CI gate validation: New molt entries form proper hash chain from prior mesh ledger.
Append-only enforcement: Prior 165 mesh entries unchanged, new entries chained forward.

Q-NF-SCHEMA-01 acceptance criteria:
  ✅ Schema doc (NF_LEDGER_SCHEMA_v1.md) published
  ✅ Unified schema resolves all 4 format incompatibilities
  ✅ molt_cycle.py reads/writes NF_LEDGER correctly
  ✅ Brier calculation implemented and tested
  ✅ Genesis record committed to main
  ⏳ specimen_intake.py integration (Phase 1 Q-SI-C1)
  ⏳ CI gate Merkle root inclusion (Phase 1, Q-MOLT-04)

